===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*ehwaz||horse}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₁éḱwos||horse}}. Cognate with {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|ehuskalk|''ehu''skalk|horse-rider|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|eha-|lang=goh}} (in personal names), Old Norse {{term|jór|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌰𐌹𐍈𐍃|tr=aihws|lang=got}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin {{term|equus|lang=la}}, Avestan {{term||tr=aspa-|lang=ae}}, Sanskrit {{term|अश्व|sc=Deva|tr=áśva|lang=sa}}, Old Armenian {{term|էշ||donkey|tr=ēš|lang=xcl}}, Tocharian A ''[[yuk]]'' B ''[[yakwe]]'', Proto-Baltic {{term/t|bat-pro|*ečwā-}} (Lithuanian ''[[ašva|ašvà]]''), Old Irish ''[[ech]]'' (Irish ''[[each]]'').

